+ * ROSEMARY (Redmi Note 10S, MT6785): GPU bring-up and identity job test.
  *
  * The Mali-G76 (Bifrost) sits at 0x13040000 behind the MFG0..MFG5 power
  * domains, which the bootloader leaves off.
@@ -10,11 +29,15 @@
  *   rosemarygpu=2  power the domains on (MFG0, MFG1 + bus protect release,
  *                  MFG2..MFG5), ungate the MFGCFG clock gate and log the Mali
  *                  identification registers
+ *   rosemarygpu=3  mode 2 + soft reset + power cores + identity job
  *
  * Reading a Mali register while its domain is off can hang a MediaTek bus,
  * so mode 2 is opt-in. The mfg_sel mux and the PLLs are left alone: the
  * identification registers are readable from the bootloader's clock.
+ *
+ * Based on hakios-xnu-kernel-mtk redwood_mali.c (Mali-G52) by HakiOS (APSL 2.0).
